The screenshot you provided shows the call to dht2​, but not the call to ds​ that creates the object  Allfwhr. Before concluding the problem lies with dht2​, I'd want to have a look at the call to ds​ and the summary output ​produced by ds​. Is truncation incorrect and wrong detections included in the ds​ output?

I don't recall that we've done anything to truncation in recent revisions.

What is the reason for using dht2​? Is it because you are trying to use the encounter rate variance calculation O2​? I'm not sure you will see improvement in the encounter rate variance estimate by using O2​ if there are only 5 detections across 31 transects.

If you want to continue this off-list, we could come back to the list when we get to the bottom of the issue.

